    "quote": "Assume that $r_{a,t} \\in [0,1], \\forall a \\in [N] $, $ T \\geq 1 $, $ \\| f^* \\|_{\\sH_{\\tilde{k}}} \\leq c $, $ \\tilde{k}(\\tilde{x},\\tilde{x}) \\leq c_{\\tilde{k}}$ and the task similarity matrix $K_Z$ is known. With probability at least $ 1-\\delta $, SupKMTL-UCB satisfies R(T) \\leq 2 \\sqrt{T} + 10 ( \\sqrt{\\frac{\\log ( 2TN(\\log(T)+1)/\\delta )}{2}} +c \\sqrt{\\lambda} ) \\sqrt{2m \\log g([T]}) \\sqrt{T \\lceil\\log(T)\\rceil} = O (\\sqrt{T \\log(g([T]))} )"
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Paper's N = K arms, c = S. m = max(1, c_k/lam). Also stated as O(sqrt(T log g([T]))). Analysis is for a modified objective without the 1/n_{a,t-1} weights. Regret R(T) uses realized rewards against per-round best arm; proof bounds E[R(T)] then applies Azuma. Theorems 2-3 bound log g([T]) by r_z r_x log(((T+1)c_k+lam)/lam) and show monotonicity in task similarity mu; not recorded separately."
